WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.900 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Our next guest is

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
a United States senator
from Montana.

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.737 line:92%
Please welcome to the show

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:05.105 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Senator Jon Tester.

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:06.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you for joining us,
Senator.

00:00:06.506 --> 00:00:08.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Good to be with you, Seth
Thank you.

00:00:08.375 --> 00:00:10.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, you are both a senato
from Montana

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:14.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the only senator
who is a working farmer.

00:00:14.814 --> 00:00:20.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
Which of those jobs --
be honest with us -- is harder

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:22.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, wow.
I mean, for me,

00:00:22.022 --> 00:00:23.156 line:92%
I think it's being a senator

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:25.058 size:84% position:42%
I mean, the truth is
there's a lot of things

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:27.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
you can't control
in production agriculture,

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
but there's a lot
of things you can't control,

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:31.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
being a United States
senator, too,

00:00:31.698 --> 00:00:34.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I would I would say
there's a bigger challenge

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:37.070 line:92%
Plus, there's so many things

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:40.106 align:start size:94% position:6%
worldwide and domestically
you have to deal with.

00:00:40.106 --> 00:00:41.374 line:92%
Yeah, it's being a U.S. senator.

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:45.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
-With that said,
you cannot be a farmer via Zoo

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:47.113 line:92%
and I think that speaks to -

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:50.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's maybe a little bit
physically harder. [ Laughs

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:51.751 line:92%
-Well, you know, yeah, it is

00:00:51.751 --> 00:00:53.653 align:start size:94% position:6%
Physically,
it is much more difficult

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:55.588 line:92%
because you're out working

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:58.091
And, by the way, the combination
of these two jobs

00:00:58.091 --> 00:01:01.461
tends to make your body hurt
at night when you go to bed.

00:01:01.461 --> 00:01:02.629 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
But it's good.

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:06.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, they're 180°° differen
in every aspect.

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:07.801 line:92%
-Is it true that you butcher

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:12.138 size:84% position:42%
and bring your own meat
from Montana to D.C.?

00:01:12.138 --> 00:01:14.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is, yes.
My wife and I ran

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:14.741 size:78% position:39% line:92%
a custom butcher shop

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:16.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the time we took over the
farm, in the late '70s,

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:19.913 align:start size:94% position:6%
'til I got in the state
legislature, in the late '90s,

00:01:19.913 --> 00:01:23.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so we tend to like to ea
the meat that we process

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:26.319
and that's what we do.
And then, I've got a beer cooler

00:01:26.319 --> 00:01:28.421 size:78% position:39%
that holds, you know,
a fair amount of beef

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:32.759
and, every month or so,
I'll bring out some meat to eat.

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:36.262
-So, we're about 100 days
into the Biden presidency.

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:39.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're obviously a Democrati
senator in a red state.

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:42.302 line:92%
How is the -- or I should say,

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:44.838
how are the progressive policies
of Joe Biden

00:01:44.838 --> 00:01:47.040 line:92%
playing back home, so far?

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:49.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, look, I think Joe's
done a great job,

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.010 align:start size:94% position:6%
especially when it comes
to the pandemic,

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:52.979 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think he's put forth
some policies

00:01:52.979 --> 00:01:56.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
that'll help middle America,
regular folks.

00:01:56.783 --> 00:02:00.687
You know, the jury is still out,
but, so far, so good.

00:02:00.687 --> 00:02:02.122 line:92%
I like what he's done, so far.

00:02:02.122 --> 00:02:04.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I will tell you
that there are folks

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:08.328
that are always going to pok
holes for political reasons.

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:09.796 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, I think,
if you look at what Joe's done

00:02:09.796 --> 00:02:12.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
in the last 100 days,
it's hard to be critical.

00:02:12.265 --> 00:02:14.067 line:92%
I think he's done a good job

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:17.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You talked, in your book,
about how, you know,

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:22.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
rural America and Democratic
you know, legislation

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:24.244 align:start size:94% position:6%
do tend to line up,
but maybe Democrats

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:27.480 size:84% position:42%
don't do a particularly
good job with messaging

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:28.781 line:92%
and it seems like rural Americ

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:32.519
has maybe just been ceded
to the Republican Party.

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:35.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
What do you think Democrat
have to do

00:02:35.355 --> 00:02:37.056 line:92%
to reconnect with rural Americ

00:02:37.056 --> 00:02:38.625 align:start size:94% position:6%
and is something
like President Biden

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:43.830 align:start size:94% position:6%
proposing rural broadband
a step in the right direction?

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, broadband
is absolutely one

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:47.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the things that we need
to really focus on

00:02:47.967 --> 00:02:53.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
because rural America
is very, very disconnected

00:02:53.273 --> 00:02:55.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are a lot of people
that are unserved,

00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:56.209 line:92%
a lot of people underserved.

00:02:56.209 --> 00:02:58.678 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got a cellphone that,
you know,

00:02:58.678 --> 00:03:01.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
it works once in a while
when I'm on the farm,

00:03:01.981 --> 00:03:02.849 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
but not very often.

00:03:02.849 --> 00:03:04.884 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, overall,
I think Democrats need to talk

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:06.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
about what they're
accomplishing a lot more

00:03:06.619 --> 00:03:09.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think we need to go
into rural America

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:10.690 line:92%
and put that message out.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, I think,
if we were able to do that

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:15.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think we'd be
a lot more successful.

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:18.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
And infrastructure,
a good place to start, Seth.

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:20.333 line:92%
And broadband's a good place

00:03:20.333 --> 00:03:22.936 align:start size:94% position:6%
to start
in the infrastructure realm.

00:03:22.936 --> 00:03:25.972
-You were one of the eight
Democratic senators to vot

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:30.710
against the federal minimum wage
increase to $15.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:32.979 line:92%
Yet, you've also advocated

00:03:32.979 --> 00:03:35.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
for increasing
the minimum wage in the past

00:03:35.582 --> 00:03:39.652 size:75% position:38%
In 2014, you thought
it you go up to $10.

00:03:39.652 --> 00:03:41.955 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why did you vote against i
and what do you --

00:03:41.955 --> 00:03:43.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
obviously,
as someone who feels like

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:44.857 align:start size:94% position:6%
it should be higher
than what it is now,

00:03:44.857 --> 00:03:46.659 line:92%
what are the next steps forward?

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:49.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I voted I voted
against the $15

00:03:49.596 --> 00:03:51.231 line:92%
because it was pretty unclear.

00:03:51.231 --> 00:03:54.133 size:81% position:41%
A lot of things in not
were not made clear,

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:56.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
like do benefits count,
for example.

00:03:56.102 --> 00:03:58.304 size:81% position:41%
And I think we ought
to encourage employers

00:03:58.304 --> 00:03:59.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
to give benefits
for their employees.

00:03:59.672 --> 00:04:01.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, that aside,
I will say this --

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:04.077 align:start size:94% position:6%
working people need to get pai
for their hard work.

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:05.445 line:92%
There's no doubt about that.

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:08.748
What the right amount is,
is much more difficult,

00:04:08.748 --> 00:04:10.617 size:84% position:42% line:92%
as you've already said.

00:04:10.617 --> 00:04:13.319 align:start size:94% position:6%
Here's why.
In rural America,

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:14.153 line:92%
you know, Manhattan, Montana

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:16.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
is a lot different
than Manhattan, New York,

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:19.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
for example,
and those small businesses

00:04:19.425 --> 00:04:20.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
mom-and-pop shops,
for the most part,

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:24.063 align:start size:94% position:6%
if they're closed down
because of this minimum wage

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:26.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's another nail
in the coffin of rural America

00:04:26.532 --> 00:04:28.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we've seen rural America
dry up

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:30.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
the last 60, 70 years,
in a big, big way.

00:04:30.870 --> 00:04:33.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I think we need
to be thoughtful about it.

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:34.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's a group,
there's a bipartisan group

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:37.443
that's coming together that,
hopefully, will come forth

00:04:37.443 --> 00:04:41.381
with a proposal that will get us
to $15 over time

00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:42.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I think that
will be something

00:04:42.315 --> 00:04:45.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
that, hopefully, we can ge
bipartisan support for.

00:04:45.718 --> 00:04:47.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I feel as though
we don't talk about,

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:51.591 size:75% position:38%
on a national stage,
Native voters much.

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:53.359 size:84% position:42% line:92%
They are a constituency

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:57.764 align:start size:94% position:6%
that has supported you
in your time in elected office

00:04:57.764 --> 00:04:58.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously,
this is not a voting bloc

00:04:58.931 --> 00:05:00.566 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's a monolith,
in any way, shape, or form

00:05:00.566 --> 00:05:04.170
but how is it that you connect
with, you know, a voting group

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:07.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we, you know, simply just
don't talk about that much

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:09.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's a pretty
well-known fact

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:11.611 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Native Americans
have a lot of challenges,

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:13.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
especially the large
land-based ones.

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:17.250
And I will tell you that, no
unlike any other voting group,

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
if you go out there
and listen to their concerns

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:22.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
and really hear them
and come back and go to work

00:05:22.722 --> 00:05:25.525 size:78% position:39%
and try to solve some
of their problems,

00:05:25.525 --> 00:05:26.359 line:92%
letting them drive the bus

00:05:26.359 --> 00:05:29.162 align:start size:94% position:6%
but letting the federal
government help them solve -

00:05:29.162 --> 00:05:32.398
whether it's unemployment issues
or clean water,

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:33.466 line:92%
I mean, issues that, by the way,

00:05:33.466 --> 00:05:36.803 align:start size:94% position:6%
affect every community
in this country --

00:05:36.803 --> 00:05:37.904 line:92%
then, they'll support you.

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:38.738 line:92%
If they know you're out there,

00:05:38.738 --> 00:05:42.208
doing your best to take care
of the problems that they have

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:45.178
they will support you and
think that's pretty well proven.

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:48.081 size:84% position:42%
It is a pretty decent
voting bloc in Montana.

00:05:48.081 --> 00:05:50.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's about 6%, 7%,
of the population,

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:51.651 size:75% position:38% line:92%
so it's significant.

00:05:51.651 --> 00:05:53.353 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, more important
than that is that,

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:56.556
if you're able to lift up some
of the unemployment problems

00:05:56.556 --> 00:05:58.291 align:start size:94% position:6%
that they have
in Indian country,

00:05:58.291 --> 00:06:00.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
it literally helps
the entire state

00:06:00.793 --> 00:06:02.662 line:92%
and helps the entire country

00:06:02.662 --> 00:06:04.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I want to finish
by asking you this.

00:06:04.497 --> 00:06:06.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
My father-in-law,
who's a wonderful man

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:12.271
and a musician who lost a couple
of fingers, still plays guitar

00:06:12.271 --> 00:06:14.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, you lost one more finge
than he did.

00:06:14.907 --> 00:06:18.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
You lost three fingers
in a farming accident, correct

00:06:18.578 --> 00:06:22.448
-Yeah, I stuck my hand in th
meat grinder at the wrong time

00:06:22.448 --> 00:06:25.151 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you never want to get
in a fight with power equipmen

00:06:25.151 --> 00:06:26.986 line:92%
because power equipment wins

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:29.989
-And, yet, you still say
being a senator is harder.

00:06:29.989 --> 00:06:31.791 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Now, I think --

00:06:31.791 --> 00:06:34.594 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that's the worst thing
you said about D.C.

00:06:34.594 --> 00:06:35.261 size:88% position:44% line:92%
in this whole interview.

00:06:35.261 --> 00:06:36.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, the thing I wanted
to get to --

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:39.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
because this is
a story of triumph --

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:43.436 align:start size:94% position:6%
you still learned how
to play trumpet, despite that.

00:06:43.436 --> 00:06:45.405 line:92%
How is that even possible?

00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:46.439 line:92%
-Well, this accident happene

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:47.840 size:78% position:39%
in between my fourth
and fifth grade year.

00:06:47.840 --> 00:06:50.810
In Big Sandy, Montana, the
started music in fifth grade

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:53.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was going to play saxophone,
to be honest.

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:54.213 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, you're missing
three digits.

00:06:54.213 --> 00:06:57.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
You aren't going to play sax
so, I took up trumpet

00:06:57.183 --> 00:07:00.920 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it worked, man.
It just worked.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:05.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, like I told my kids
and like my parents told me,

00:07:05.224 --> 00:07:06.292 line:92%
you got to be good at somethin

00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:08.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I was a pretty decent
trumpet player,

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:09.662 size:84% position:42% line:92%
at one time in my life,

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:11.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it propelled me
through college.

00:07:11.631 --> 00:07:13.666 size:81% position:41%
And, quite honestly,
when I started running

00:07:13.666 --> 00:07:16.035
for the state legislature,
I brought my horn with me

00:07:16.035 --> 00:07:18.671 size:84% position:42%
and played a few tunes
when it was appropriate

00:07:18.671 --> 00:07:21.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it helped me
in electoral politics, too

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:22.809 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
so it's been good.

00:07:22.809 --> 00:07:24.510 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't think
I'd be a U.S. senator

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:28.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
without my music, that's bee
in my past, for sure.

00:07:28.681 --> 00:07:31.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that is truly
a story of perseverance.

00:07:31.484 --> 00:07:33.386 size:78% position:39%
Thanks for sharing it
and thanks so much

00:07:33.386 --> 00:07:34.921 line:92%
for making time for us today

00:07:34.921 --> 00:07:36.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, Seth,
always a pleasure.

00:07:36.522 --> 00:07:38.191 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Thank you very much.

